hadiths[152]{hadithnumber,text}:
"129001","Yahya related to me from Malik from a reliable source from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his father's father that the Messenger of Allah"
"129002","Yahya related to me from Malik from a reliable source from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his father's father that the Messenger of Allah"
"129101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"129102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"129201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm that Aban ibn Uthman and Hisham ibn Ismail used to mention in their khutbas built-in liability agreements in the sale of slaves"
"129202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm that Aban ibn Uthman and Hisham ibn Ismail used to mention in their khutbas built-in liability agreements in the sale of slaves"
"129301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Umar sold one of his slaves for eight hundred dirhams with the stipulation that he was not responsible for defects. The person who bought the slave complained to Abdullah ibn Umar that the slave had a disease which he had not told him about. They argued and went to Uthman ibn Affan for a decision . The man said"
"129302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Umar sold one of his slaves for eight hundred dirhams with the stipulation that he was not responsible for defects. The person who bought the slave complained to Abdullah ibn Umar that the slave had a disease which he had not told him about. They argued and went to Uthman ibn Affan for a decision . The man said"
"129401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud told him that Abdullah ibn Masud bought a slave-girl from his wife"
"129402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud told him that Abdullah ibn Masud bought a slave-girl from his wife"
"129501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would say"
"129502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would say"
"129601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Abdullah ibn Amir gave Uthman ibn Affan a slave-girl who had a husband whom he had purchased at Basra. Uthman said"
"129602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Abdullah ibn Amir gave Uthman ibn Affan a slave-girl who had a husband whom he had purchased at Basra. Uthman said"
"129701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf that Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf bought a slave- girl and found that she had a husband"
"129702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf that Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf bought a slave- girl and found that she had a husband"
"129801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"129802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"129901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"129902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"130001","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah"
"130002","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah"
"130101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'r-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Haritha from his mother"
"130102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'r-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Haritha from his mother"
"130201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit that Zayd ibn Thabit did not sell fruit until the Pleiades were visible"
"130202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit that Zayd ibn Thabit did not sell fruit until the Pleiades were visible"
"130301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah"
"130302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah"
"130401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Said ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujra from his paternal aunt, Zaynab bint Kab ibn Ujra that al-Furaya bint Malik ibn Sinan, the sister of Abu Said al-Khudri, informed her that she went to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and asked to be able to return to her people among the Banu Khudra since her husband had gone out in search of some of his slaves who had run away and he had caught up with them near al-Qudum, (which is 6 miles from Madina), and they had killed him. She said, ""I asked the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, if I could return to my people in the Banu Khudra, as my husband had not left me in a dwelling which belonged to him, and had left me no maintenance. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said,'Yes.' So I left. When I was in the courtyard, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, called me or summoned me, and I answered him. He said, 'What did you say?' I repeated the story about my husband. He said, 'Stay in your house until what is written reaches its term.' I did the idda in the house for four months and ten days."" She added, ""When Uthman ibn Affan sent for me, I told him that, and he followed it and made decisions by it."""""""
"130402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Da'ud ibn al-Husayn from Abu Sufyan"
"130501","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abu'r-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman heard his mother"
"130502","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abu'r-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman heard his mother"
"130601","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz decided in a case to make a reduction for crop damage. Malik said"
"130602","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz decided in a case to make a reduction for crop damage. Malik said"
"130701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abd ar-Rahman that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad would sell produce from his orchard and keep some of it aside"
"130702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abd ar-Rahman that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad would sell produce from his orchard and keep some of it aside"
"130801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr that his grandfather"
"130802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr that his grandfather"
"130901","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, that he heard Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say: Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik separated men from their wives, and these women were mothers of children of men who had died, and they married them after one or two menstrual cycles. He separated them until they completed their waiting period of four months and ten days. Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said: Glorified is Allah! Allah says in His Book: \And those of you who die and leave wives...\"" (2:234) - they are not wives."""""""
"130902","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab: Abdullah ibn Amir gifted a slave girl to Uthman ibn Affan, who had a husband. He had bought her in Basra. Uthman said: \I will not approach her until her husband divorces her.\"" Ibn Amir appeased her husband"
"131001","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that Ata ibn Yasar said"
"131002","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that Ata ibn Yasar said"
"131101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd al-Hamid ibn Suhayl ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Said al- Khudri and from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"131102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd al-Hamid ibn Suhayl ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Said al- Khudri and from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"131201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Yazid that Zayd ibn Ayyash told him that he had once asked Sad ibn Abi Waqqas about selling white wheat for a type of good barley. Sad asked him which was the better and when he told him the white wheat"
"131202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Yazid that Zayd ibn Ayyash told him that he had once asked Sad ibn Abi Waqqas about selling white wheat for a type of good barley. Sad asked him which was the better and when he told him the white wheat"
"131301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"131302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"131401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban that Ibn Muhayriz said, ""I went into the mosque and saw Abu Said al-Khudri and so I sat by him and asked him about coitus interruptus. Abu Said al-Khudri said, 'We went out with the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, on the expedition to the Banu al-Mustaliq. We took some Arabs prisoner, and we desired the women as celibacy was hard for us. We wanted the ransom, so we wanted to practise coitus interruptus. We said, 'Shall we practise coitus interruptus while the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, is among us before we ask him?' We asked him about that and he said, 'You don't have to not do it. There is no self which is to come into existence up to the Day of Rising but that it will come into existence.' """""""
"131402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Da'ud ibn al-Husayn from Abu Sufyan"
"131501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab that the Messenger of Allah"
"131502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab that the Messenger of Allah"
"131601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu al-Nadr, the freed slave of Umar ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Aflah, the freed slave of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from a freed slave woman of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari that he used to practice coitus interruptus ('azl)."
"131602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi' from Abdullah ibn Umar from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession to the owner of an 'ariyya (date palms given for temporary use) to sell it by estimation (khars)."
"131701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Musa ibn Abi Tamim from Abu'l Hubab Said ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"131702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Musa ibn Abi Tamim from Abu'l Hubab Said ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"131801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abu Said al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah"
"131802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abu Said al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah"
"131901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd ibn Qays al-Makki that Mujahid said"
"131902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd ibn Qays al-Makki that Mujahid said"
"132001","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Humayd ibn Nafi that Zaynab bint Abi Salama related these three traditions to him. Zaynab said, ""I visited Umm Habiba, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when her father Abu Sufyan ibn Harb had died. Umm Habiba called for a yellowy perfume perhaps khaluq or something else. She rubbed the perfume first on a slave-girl and she then wiped it on the sides of her face and said, 'By Allah! I have no need of perfume but I heard the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, say, 'It is not halal for a woman who trusts in Allah and the Last Day to abstain from adornment in mourning for someone who has died, for more than three nights, except for four months and ten days for a husband.' """""""
"132002","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard from his grandfather"
"132101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar that Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan sold a gold or silver drinking- vessel for more than its weight. Abu'dDarda said"
"132102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar that Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan sold a gold or silver drinking- vessel for more than its weight. Abu'dDarda said"
"132201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"132202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"132301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"132302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"132401","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Oasim ibn Muhammad said"
"132402","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Oasim ibn Muhammad said"
"132501","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abu'z-Zinad heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say"
"132502","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abu'z-Zinad heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say"
"132601","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say"
"132602","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say"
"132701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Malik ibn Aus ibn al-Hadathan an-Nasri that one time he asked to exchange 100 dinars. He said"
"132702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Malik ibn Aus ibn al-Hadathan an-Nasri that one time he asked to exchange 100 dinars. He said"
"132801","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt saw Said ibn al-Musayyab sell gold counterpoising for gold. He poured his gold into one pan of the scales"
"132802","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt saw Said ibn al-Musayyab sell gold counterpoising for gold. He poured his gold into one pan of the scales"
"132901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"132902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"133001","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"133002","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"133101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"133102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"133201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Hakim ibn Hizam traded in food for people as Umar ibn al-Khattab had ordered him to do. Hakim re-sold the food before he had taken delivery of it. That reached Umar ibn al-Khattab and he revoked the sale and said"
"133202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Hakim ibn Hizam traded in food for people as Umar ibn al-Khattab had ordered him to do. Hakim re-sold the food before he had taken delivery of it. That reached Umar ibn al-Khattab and he revoked the sale and said"
"133301","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that receipts were given to people in the time of Marwan ibn al-Hakam for the produce of the market at al-Jar. People bought and sold the receipts among themselves before they took delivery of the goods. Zayd Thabit and one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah"
"133302","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that receipts were given to people in the time of Marwan ibn al-Hakam for the produce of the market at al-Jar. People bought and sold the receipts among themselves before they took delivery of the goods. Zayd Thabit and one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah"
"133401","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man wanted to buy food from a man in advance. The man who wanted to sell the food to him went with him to the market"
"133402","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man wanted to buy food from a man in advance. The man who wanted to sell the food to him went with him to the market"
"133501","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard Jamil ibn Abd ar-Rahman the Muadhdhin say to Said ibn al-Musayyab"
"133502","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard Jamil ibn Abd ar-Rahman the Muadhdhin say to Said ibn al-Musayyab"
"133601","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abu'z-Zinad heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab andSulayman ibn Yasar forbid a man to sell wheat for gold on delayed terms and then to buy dried dates with the gold before he had taken delivery of the gold"
"133602","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abu'z-Zinad heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab andSulayman ibn Yasar forbid a man to sell wheat for gold on delayed terms and then to buy dried dates with the gold before he had taken delivery of the gold"
"133701","Yahya related to me from Malik that Kathir ibn Farqad asked Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm about a man who sold food to be delivered at a future date to a man for gold and then with the gold"
"133702","Yahya related to me from Malik that Kathir ibn Farqad asked Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm about a man who sold food to be delivered at a future date to a man for gold and then with the gold"
"1338","[1338] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, that he heard Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab say: There is no usury except in gold or silver. Or what is measured or weighed, with what is eaten or drunk.\\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 1338 Arabic Hadith:"
"133901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said that there was no harm in a man making an advance to another man for food"
"133902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said that there was no harm in a man making an advance to another man for food"
"134001","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Sulayman ibn Yasar said"
"134002","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Sulayman ibn Yasar said"
"134101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Sulayman ibn Yasar told him that one time the fodder of the animals of Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth was finished so he said to his slave"
"134102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Sulayman ibn Yasar told him that one time the fodder of the animals of Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth was finished so he said to his slave"
"134201","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard the same as that from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Ibn Muayqib ad-Dawsi. Malik said"
"134202","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard the same as that from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Ibn Muayqib ad-Dawsi. Malik said"
"134301","Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam asked Said ibn al-Musayyab's advice. \\""I am a man who buys food with receipts from al-Jar. Perhaps I will buy something for a dinar and half a dirham"""""""
"134302","Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam asked Said ibn al-Musayyab's advice. \\""I am a man who buys food with receipts from al-Jar. Perhaps I will buy something for a dinar and half a dirham"""""""
"134401","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Muhammad Sirin used to say"
"134402","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Muhammad Sirin used to say"
"134501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal that he said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me from A'isha, the Mother of the Believers, from Judama bint Wahb al-Asadiyya that she informed her that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""I intended to forbid al-ghila (sexual intercourse while breastfeeding), but then I recalled that the Romans and Persians do that and it does not harm their children."""""""
"134502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi' that Hakim ibn Hizam purchased food which Umar ibn al-Khattab had ordered for the people. Hakim sold the food before he had taken possession of it. That reached Umar ibn al-Khattab, so he revoked it and said: ""Do not sell food which you have purchased until you take possession of it."""""""
"134601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yunus ibn Yusuf from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab passed by Hatab ibn Abi Baltaa who was underselling some of his raisins in the market. Umar ibn al- Khattab said to him"
"134602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yunus ibn Yusuf from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab passed by Hatab ibn Abi Baltaa who was underselling some of his raisins in the market. Umar ibn al- Khattab said to him"
"1347","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Uthman ibn Affan forbade hoarding"
"1348","Yahya related to me from Malik from Salih ibn Kaysan from Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib that Ali ibn Abi Talib sold one of his camels called Usayfir for 20 camels to be delivered later"
"1349","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar bought a female riding-camel for four camels and he guaranteed to give them in full to the buyer at ar-Rabadha"
"1350","Yahya related to me that Malik asked Ibn Shihab about selling animals"
"1351","Yahya related to me from Malih from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"1352","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Said ibn al- Musayyab said"
"1353","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Said ibn al-Musayyab that the Messenger of Allah"
"1354","Yahya related to me from Malik from Da'ud ibn al-Husayn that he heard Said ibn alMusayyab say"
"1355","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad that Said ibn al- Musayyab said"
"1356","Malik said, ""It is the generally agreed on way of doing things among us that the meat of camels, cattle, sheep and so on is not to be bartered one for one, except like for like, weight for weight, from hand to hand. There is no harm in that. If it is not weighed, then it is estimated to be like for like from hand to hand."" Malik said, ""There is no harm in bartering the meat of fish for the meat of camels, cattle, and sheep and so on two or more for one, from hand to hand. If delayed terms enter the transaction however, there is no good in it."" Malik said, ""I think that poultry is different from the meat of cattle and fish. I see no harm in selling some of it for something different, more of one than another, from hand to hand. None of that is to be sold on delayed terms."" Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from Abu Masud al-Ansari that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute and the earnings of a fortune teller. By the earnings of a prostitute he meant what a woman was given for fornication. The earnings of a fortune teller were what he was given to tell a fortune. Malik said, ""I disapprove of the price of a dog, whether it is a hunting dog or otherwise because the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, forbade the price of a dog"
"1357","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"1358","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said"
"1359","Malik said, ""The generally agreed on way of doing things among us about whatever is weighed but is not gold or silver, i.e. copper, brass, lead, black lead, iron, herbs, figs, cotton, and any such things that are weighed, is that there is no harm in bartering all those sorts of things two for one, hand to hand. There is no harm in taking a ritl of iron for two ritls of iron, and a ritl of brass for two ritls of brass."" Malik said, ""There is no good in two for one of one sort with delayed terms. There is no harm in taking two of one sort for one of another on delayed terms, if the two sorts are clearly different. If both sorts resemble each other but their names are different, like lead and black lead, brass and yellow brass, I disapprove of taking two of one sort for one of the other on delayed terms."" Malik said, ""When buying something of this nature, there is no harm in selling It beforetaking possession of it to some one other than the person from whom it was purchased, if the price is taken immediately and if it was bought originally by measure or weight. If it was bought without measuring, it should be sold to someone other than the person from whom it was bought, for cash or with delayed terms. That is because goods have to be guaranteed when they are bought without measuring, and they cannot be guaranteed when bought by weight until they are weighed and the deal is completed. This is the best of what I have heard about all these things. It is what people continue to do among us."" Malik said, ""The way of doing things among us with what is measured or weighed of things which are not eaten or drunk, like safflower, date-stones, fodder leaves, indigo dye and the like of that is that there is no harm in bartering all those sort of things two for one, hand to hand. Do not take two for one from the same variety with delayed terms. If the types are clearly different, there is no harm in taking two of one for one of the other with delayed terms. There is no harm in selling whatever is purchased of all these sorts, before taking delivery of them if the price is taken from someone other than the person from whom they were purchased."" Malik said, ""Anything of any variety that profits people, like gravel and gypsum, one quantity of them for two of its like with delayed terms is usury. One quantity of both of them for its equal plus any increase with delayed terms, is usury."" Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, forbade two sales in one sale"
"1360","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man said to another"
"1361","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad was asked about a man who bought goods for 10 dinars cash or fifteen dinars on credit. He disapproved of that and forbade it. Malik said that if a man bought goods from a man for either 10 dinars or 15 dinars on credit"
"1362","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar from Said ibn al-Musayyab that the Messenger of Allah"
"1363","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban and from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"1364","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of the fetus of a fetus (habal al-habalah). This was a transaction that the people of the Jahiliyyah used to engage in. A man would buy a she-camel until the she-camel gave birth, and then the offspring within her belly gave birth."
"1365","Malik related to me that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Masud used to relate that the Messenger of Allah"
"1366","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from Busr ibn Said from Ubayd"
"1367","Yahya related to me from Malik from Uthman ibn Hafs ibn Khalda from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Umar was asked about a man who took a loan from another man for a set term. The creditor reduced the debt"
"1368","And it was narrated to me, from Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab: He used to say: It is forbidden to sell an animal for meat. Abu al-Zinad said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab: What do you say about a man who buys an old ewe for ten sheep? Sa'id said: If he bought it to slaughter it, then there is no good in that. Abu al-Zinad said: And everyone I met among the people forbade selling an animal for meat. Abu al-Zinad said: And this used to be written in the covenants of the governors during the time of Aban ibn Uthman and Hisham ibn Ismail, forbidding that."
